    "created_at": "2021-03-10T09:51:43Z",
    "updated_at": "2021-03-10T09:51:43Z",
    "body": "> So, IIUC this means that the manifest is picked once based on the initial media properties and then doesn't change for the document. Is that correct?\r\n\r\nAt \"install/use time\". \r\n\r\n> What happens if a PWA is installed under some conditions and then opened under others? Would it have the wrong manifest?\r\n\r\nPotentially, yes. \"Updating\" is still undefined behavior across UAs, because some create shortcuts and make policy decisions at the OS level at install time. \r\n\r\n> (e.g. would I have a different splash screen if I installed the PWA after dark when my phone switches to dark mode vs. if I installed it at noon, when my phone is in light mode?)\r\n\r\nYeah, that's basically what brought us here:\r\nhttps://github.com/w3c/manifest/issues/955\r\n\r\nAnd related Chrome bug:\r\nhttps://bugs.chromium.org/p/chromium/issues/detail?id=970159\r\n\r\nFirst step was to at least get consistent `media=` behavior across UAs. We've not sorted out when different dark/light modes should apply and if that should be defined at the manifest level, in HTML, or in even in the screenshot itself (e.g., an SVG file could have its own media rules). \r\n\r\n",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "reactions": {
